# Impostor Syndrome ({4}{U}{U}): "Whenever a nontoken creature you control deals combat damage to a player, create a token that's a copy
# of it, except it isn't legendary." (CR 510.2, 603.2, 707.2, 707.9b, 111.1.) Marwyn, the Clearcutter (legendary, 2/1) is cast on
# turn 1; on turn 3 the Syndrome comes down (Black Lotus and the three Moxen pay) and he attacks: a copy token that is not
# legendary (so the legend rule leaves both, CR 704.5j), Bot2 at 18. On turn 5 both attack: the nontoken one makes another token, the
# token's damage makes nothing (CR 111.7): three Marwyns, Bot2 at 14.

